From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:47:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple-g5p: refuse system sleep until GPU resume works

On J71t a completed suspend/resume cycle does not bring the GPU back,
yet the sleep admission admits a parked, idle GPU and
/sys/power/suspend_ready reads "ready", so userspace that follows the
kernel's answer suspends into a GPU that does not come back.

Add a read-only "suspend" module parameter, off by default. While it is
off, the G5P sleep admission refuses before anything is shut: prepare
logs why and how to opt in and returns -EOPNOTSUPP, and the readiness
check answers "resume-unsupported", so /sys/power/suspend_ready reads
"not-ready <gpu>:resume-unsupported -95". Booting with
a9_gpu_drm.suspend=1 admits sleep exactly as before, for work on
resume. Boards without the G5P driver are not affected.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc
index bb3ead784..5f96de133 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc
@@ -24,6 +24,18 @@
  * render attachment per boot), so it says nothing about work in flight.
  * Accepted jobs not yet signalled are r8_queued.
  */
+
+/*
+ * GPU resume does not work yet: on J71t a completed suspend/resume cycle did
+ * not bring the GPU back. Until it does, system sleep is refused at admission,
+ * so /sys/power/suspend_ready and every suspend attempt name the GPU instead
+ * of suspending into a GPU that does not come back. suspend=1 admits sleep
+ * exactly as before, for work on resume.
+ */
+static bool g5p_suspend;
+module_param_named(suspend, g5p_suspend, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(suspend, "Admit system sleep although GPU resume does not work yet (default: off)");
+
 enum {
 	G5P_SB_COMPUTE,		/* no CDM stamp certificate yet (lane GS) */
 	G5P_SB_TERMINAL,
@@ -277,6 +289,11 @@ static int g5p_system_sleep_prepare(struct device *dev)
 	int ret = -EBUSY, users;
 
 	/* Every refusal below names its stage and reason: no silent -EBUSY. */
+	if (!g5p_suspend) {
+		dev_info(dev, "GPU-PM sleep refused: stage=entry why=resume-unsupported: GPU resume is not supported yet; boot with %s.suspend=1 to try it\n",
+			 KBUILD_MODNAME);
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	}
 	if (!g || !g->event_cookie || !g->boot) {
 		dev_info(dev, "GPU-PM sleep refused: stage=entry why=%s\n",
 			 !g ? "no-core" : !g->event_cookie ? "no-drm" : "no-boot");
@@ -463,6 +480,8 @@ static int g5p_system_sleep_check(struct device *dev)
 		return -ENODEV;
 	d = g->event_cookie;
 	d->sleep_why[0] = 0;
+	if (!g5p_suspend)
+		return g5p_sleep_why(d, -EOPNOTSUPP, "resume-unsupported");
 	b = READ_ONCE(g->boot);
 	if (READ_ONCE(g->sleep_failed))
 		return g5p_sleep_why(d, -EIO, "sleep-failed");
